**Genetic Engineering Research and Medical Device Patent Overview**

In 2023, BioInnovate Solutions, headquartered in Cambridge, MA, has made significant strides in genetic engineering and medical devices. Our research team, led by Dr. Emily Tran, has focused on developing CRISPR-Cas9-based therapies aimed at rare genetic disorders. Collaborating with the Massachusetts Institute of Technology (MIT) and Harvard Medical School, our efforts have yielded promising results in preclinical trials for conditions like cystic fibrosis and Duchenne muscular dystrophy. 

To protect our innovations, we have filed several patents, including US Patent 11,234,567, which covers our novel gene-editing delivery mechanism using biodegradable nanoparticles. This technology has been co-developed with NanoMed Solutions.

